

{%- liquid
  assign product_has_swatches = false
  for product_option in closest.product.options_with_values
    assign swatch_count = product_option.values | map: 'swatch' | compact | size
    if swatch_count > 0
      assign product_has_swatches = true
      break
    endif
  endfor
-%}

{% capture product_card_children %}
  <div class="featured-product-content-top">
    {% content_for 'block', type: 'product-title', id: 'featured-product-title' %}

    {% content_for 'block', type: '_featured-product-price', id: 'featured-product-price' %}
  </div>
  {% content_for 'block', type: '_featured-product-gallery', id: 'featured-product-gallery' %}
  {% if product_has_swatches %}
    <div class="featured-product-content-bottom">
      {%- content_for 'block', type: 'swatches', id: 'featured-product-swatches' -%}
    </div>
  {% endif %}
  {%- comment -%}
    Stock Horizon's _featured-product block ships as a title/price/gallery/
    swatches-only showcase card with no way to add a variant-picker or buy
    button -- it has no {% content_for 'blocks' %} slot, so a merchant can't
    add those from the theme editor either. The bespoke ona-featured-product.liquid
    this replaces lets a shopper pick a variant and add to cart right on the
    home page; dropping that here would be a real functionality regression,
    not just a visual one. Extending this vendored block with description +
    variant-picker + buy-buttons (the same block types the PDP's own native
    buy box already uses) keeps that capability using real Horizon components
    instead of reintroducing a bespoke hand-rolled cart form.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="featured-product-content-description">
    {% content_for 'block', type: 'product-description', id: 'featured-product-description' %}
  </div>
  <div class="featured-product-content-buy">
    {% content_for 'block', type: 'variant-picker', id: 'featured-product-variant-picker' %}
    {% content_for 'block', type: 'buy-buttons', id: 'featured-product-buy-buttons' %}
    {%- comment -%}
      Appstle (subscriptions app) does not auto-detect an arbitrary native
      buy-buttons form -- confirmed by testing: without this span, the native
      buy box here renders a plain one-time-purchase Add to cart with no
      subscription options, even though Appstle's script is loaded on the
      page. ona-product-information.liquid's PDP buy box works today only
      because Appstle finds ITS OWN matching hook there (not verified exactly
      how -- out of scope for this section). This snippet's OWN sibling
      section (ona-featured-product.liquid, the bespoke one this replaces)
      already carries this exact selector and correctly shows subscription
      options, so reuse the same proven hook rather than guess at a new one.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <span class="appstle_stand_alone_selector" data-product-handle="{{ closest.product.handle }}" style="display:none;"></span>
  </div>
{% endcapture %}

{% render 'product-card', children: product_card_children, product: closest.product, product_card_gap: 8 %}

{% stylesheet %}
  .featured-product-content-top {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: var(--gap-sm);
  }
{% endstylesheet %}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "t:names.product",
  "tag": null,
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "t:content.resource_reference_product_card"
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    { "type": "product-title" },
    { "type": "_featured-product-price" },
    { "type": "_featured-product-gallery" },
    { "type": "swatches" },
    { "type": "product-description" },
    { "type": "variant-picker" },
    { "type": "buy-buttons" }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
